  "id": "Compound::DB00590 - Gene::90134",
  "verbalization": "Doxazosin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Floppy Iris Syndrome, which is mediated through Prazosin. Prazosin, in turn, binds to Kcnh7, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Doxazosin influences Kcnh7. The evidence is consistent across two paths, with both linking Doxazosin to Prazosin, which then binds to Kcnh7. The lowest common ancestors for Doxazosin and Prazosin are both categorized under \"Agent Affecting Cardiovascular System\" and \"Oxacycle,\" indicating a shared biological context. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role of Prazosin in modulating Kcnh7 activity, potentially through a mechanism involving oxacycle compounds. The relationship between Doxazosin and Kcnh7 is thus supported by a chain of interactions involving Prazosin and the Kcnh7 receptor, with the oxacycle class serving as a common intermediary.",
